From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:24:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: qcom: camss: raise the VFE clock for a route added
 later

The VFE clock rate is chosen when the first route powers the VFE up. A
route added while the VFE is running only checks the current rate and
fails the power up with -EBUSY when it is too slow. On MSM8226, starting
the IMX132 (39.6 Mpixel/s) first sets a rate the IMX179 (259.2 Mpixel/s)
cannot use, so the second camera can only start if it was started first.

Raise the clock to the rate the routes now need instead of failing.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 84f471cca..2de281798 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -1109,6 +1109,9 @@ int vfe_get(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 		vfe->res->hw_ops->hw_version(vfe);
 	} else {
 		ret = vfe_check_clock_rates(vfe);
+		/* A route added to a running VFE may need a faster clock. */
+		if (ret == -EBUSY)
+			ret = vfe_set_clock_rates(vfe);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			goto error_pm_domain;
 	}
